WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
Good morning John.

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:03.050
So in your last video, you were like, 'You
owe us a punishment!'

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:04.050
and I was like, 'I do?'

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.770
We've been doing this for a long time, and
there have been a lot of punishable infractions,

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:06.899
so it's getting kinda confusing.

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:11.140
Luckily, a bunch of nerdfighters, led by the
indestructible Valerie2776, have created a

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:15.010
spreadsheet in which all of our punishments
and the reasons why we had them have been

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:16.010
listed.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.280
And now, as a reminder, and also a history
lesson, and also to figure what the heck is

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.890
going on, I am converting the spreadsheet
into a video, and because I do not wanna get

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:21.960
punished I'm going very fast.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:24.900
On January 1st, 2007, we created this channel
with three rules:

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.590
1) You have to make a video on your day.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:28.490
2) The video can't be longer than four minutes
long.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:31.039
and 3) Hank and John Green cannot communicate
textually.

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:34.929
The first rule was broken that very same month
when John, you CCed me on an email to someone

00:00:34.929 --> 00:00:36.620
else, which counted as textual communication.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:37.899
You had to wax your chin.

00:00:37.899 --> 00:00:38.899
John: AAAAUAAAHHHH!

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:42.449
Hank: Later, I did the exact same thing, CCing
John, and had to re-enact three of my most

00:00:42.449 --> 00:00:44.030
embarrassing moments with sock puppets.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:47.559
I also once wrote 'See you tomorrow' in text
in the end of a video.

00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:48.559
Ugh!

00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:51.659
As a result, I had to go out on the streets
of Missoula and try to give away Peeps, which

00:00:51.659 --> 00:00:53.579
is how I met Kurt the Punk-Rock Nerdfighter.

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:55.780
In July, I just IMed you.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.049
And then, you replied, so we both got punished.

00:00:59.049 --> 00:01:02.059
We did a shared punishment, both dressing
up like the most embarrassing picture we could

00:01:02.059 --> 00:01:03.059
find from high school.

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:06.810
In March, you missed a video because you were
hospitalized and you accidentally replied

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:10.591
to me on a forum, and so you had to eat a
blenderized Happy Meal, wax your legs, and

00:01:10.591 --> 00:01:11.591
lick a cat.

00:01:11.591 --> 00:01:14.659
I'm not sure why there were three, possibly
something about donations to Daniel Biss's

00:01:14.659 --> 00:01:15.659
campaign.

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:19.320
Finally, in December of 2007 during the first
Project for Awesome, I replied to a comment

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.640
you left on a Project for Awesome video, and
thus had to blend together Peeps and Strawberry

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:29.700
Hill flavored citrus wine and drink it while
playing a show to six people, none of whom

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.340
knew me, except for my wife.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:32.340
My first show ever!

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:35.990
For the rest of Vlogbrothers, we abolished
the textual communication rule, so now John

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:37.390
and I can email each other, which is helpful.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.670
We've also altered the schedule in various
different ways and made time limit exemptions

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:45.180
for educational videos, videos with montages
in them, and videos that are 4 minutes and

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.740
1 second long because YouTube adds a second.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.740
Why, YouTube?

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:49.740
Why do you add a second?

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:53.680
In April 2008, I made a video that was 14
seconds too long; I don't know why, I just,

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.850
ah, messed up that week.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:59.240
As a result, I had to sing the song 'World
Wide Web Girl' with pigtails in my hair.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.219
Then in October, I accidentally put 30 seconds
of nothingness on the end of my video, which

00:02:03.219 --> 00:02:06.729
resulted in me dancing around my house dressed
like Carrie Bradshaw from Sex and the City

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:08.520
with singing Rick Astley's 'Never Gonna Give
You Up'.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.720
[music/singing "never gonna make you cry,
never gonna say goodbye"]

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:12.720
The infamous Hankroll.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:17.930
In June of 2008, you missed a video, and had
to eat a sandwich made out of lard and protein

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:18.930
meal.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:19.930
Bleurgh!

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:23.330
Then in November, I made a video that was
2 seconds too long and had to spend 15 hours

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.330
in a Target.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.330
[Hank ventriloquizing cans] Ahh!

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:26.330
Ahh!

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.330
Ahh!

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:28.330
Ahhhhh!

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.330
During VidCon 2010, both of us failed to upload
our videos.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:32.860
The videos in response to that were your amazing
'Fitness for Nerds' video and my Katniss Everdeen

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:33.860
make-up tutorial.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:37.260
In 2011 a long-standing agreement to be punished
if Helen Hunt ever saw my 'Helen Hunt' video

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:38.260
came to fruition.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:41.040
She sent me a tweet, and then I had to hump
my entire town.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:45.150
In 2012, there were no punishments, but there
may have been some punishable infractions,

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.550
I'll get to that soon.

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:50.590
In 2013, the very first punishment dealt to
someone who wasn't you or me, was dealt to

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:53.640
Grace Helbig for making a video longer than
4 minutes during your paternity leave.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:57.410
It was not entirely clear whether the rules
applied to her; she slapped herself anyway.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:01.600
And John, in October of 2013, you made a longer
than 4 minute video that was deemed to not

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:04.780
be educational enough, and so you were punished.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.950
You ate slobber carrots, made by your son.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:10.330
Here's where it gets confusing, and someone
will eventually clear this up, but it is very

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:13.990
clear in 2012 we both owed punishments.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:17.790
I can't figure out what they were for, but
I know that there were punishments, because

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:20.000
on October 28th, you made a bet with Nerdfighteria.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.970
You said that both you and I had outstanding
punishments, but if we could get to a thousand

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:28.060
videos before Nerdfighteria loaned a million
dollars through Kiva.org, those punishments

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.100
would be wiped clean.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.071
However, if they got to a million dollars
first, we would double our punishments; we

00:03:33.071 --> 00:03:34.071
would both have two.

00:03:34.071 --> 00:03:37.530
Of course, never underestimate Nerdfighteria,
a million dollars was indeed loaned.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:39.180
And so we each had two punishments.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:45.510
We absolved one of them, by doing six videos
in a week, three each, which leaves, finally,

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:46.510
one punishment each.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:48.770
It was your own doing, John; you can't complain.

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.680
John, I got a really good idea from the comments
for your video about what my punishment's

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:56.590
gonna be, so everybody, leave comments for
what John's gonna do in his punishment!

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.510
And John, I will see you on Tuesday.

